      ":question/id": "734533ce-b712-5633-8707-4b3a0dd218b9",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $BA+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-16 & 2 \\sqrt{3} & - 3 \\sqrt{7} \\\\ - \\sqrt{5} & - 3 \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nBA+BC=B(A+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA+BC & =B(A+C) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-16 & 2 \\sqrt{3} & - 3 \\sqrt{7} \\\\ - \\sqrt{5} & - 3 \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
