    "question": {
      ":question/id": "264fc614-ea67-55ce-b561-e5c24a9ac258",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 15\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n|  |  | $-12$ | $-9$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-3}} | $15$ |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =A{I}_{3} \\\\  & =A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
